herd Ronny, Lee is confronted by a particularly mouthy motorist, Liam arrests a man who denies carrying out a shocking attack, tasers are drawn after a van driver causes carnage.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-04-30\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Episode 2\",\"overview\":\"Interceptor Spike takes the lead against a runaway car thief in one of the most challenging pursuits ever. Liam investigates a gang of suspected drug dealers. A  supposedly straightforward stop snowballs into a showdown with an aggressive youngster.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-05-07\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Episode 3\",\"overview\":\"Paul `Jacko' Jackson is forced to draw his Taser, while dog handler Mo pursues two stolen cars through the streets of Middlesbrough. Steve runs after an uninsured driver who has ditched his car, and Halloween turns from fright night to fight night.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-05-14\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Episode 4\",\"overview\":\"Damo is involved in a high speed pursuit, but the driver manages to give him the slip. The interceptors' eye in the sky then spots five runners from a crashed car. Dog handler Mo is called to a mansion, and Jacko tackles an angry mob.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-05-21\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Episode 5\",\"overview\":\"Rookie interceptor Rachael faces a baptism of fire including a chase with a pregnant passenger, and a deluded motorist calls the police to report interceptor Chris for stealing.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-05-28\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Episode 6\",\"overview\":\"A failure to stop in Hartlepool turns into an armed stand-off in a full-blown kidnapping situation, while a 14-year-old boy is found in possession of a bag of crack cocaine, cash and a knife. Lee goes on a high-speed pursuit through Stockton, and Jacko and Simon tackle a drug driver who is wearing a balaclava.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-06-04\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Episode 7\",\"overview\":\"AJ and Richie are in pursuit of a van speeding through narrow country lanes, while Jacko and the team box in a van carrying large quantities of cannabis. Plus, sparks fly when dog handler Justin and police dog Elsa capture two burglars on a building site.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-06-11\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Episode 8\",\"overview\":\"During a dramatic pursuit, Faulko is rammed off the road at 80mph and has to be rushed to hospital, while the team battles to tackle the aftermath of the crash, and track down the driver responsible. Meanwhile, timing is everything as Liam locks up a rogue biker with the help of patience, pepper spray and the actions of a heroic passer-by.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-06-25\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Episode 9\",\"overview\":\"Dog handler Darren calls on all his powers of persuasions to try to end a roof-top stand-off, while Steve is forced to use his pepper spray when a suspect refuses to come quietly. Plus, there is a tense stand-off with a man armed with a knife.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-07-09\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Episode 10\",\"overview\":\"Chris and the team are in pursuit of a stolen Mazda M3, but the driver disappears into an industrial area and tracker dog Ronny tries to track down the villain. Meanwhile, a routine stop and search takes a dangerous turn for Jimmy, and Liam helps take down a banned driver who causes carnage at a red light.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-07-16\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Episode 11\",\"overview\":\"Jacko is tired on by a suspect with a gun, while it is a day and the beach for Spike as he hunts for a man on a quad bike with a gun. Liam and Lee arrest a drugged up likely lass who could give Pinocchio lessons in telling lies.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-07-23\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Episode 12\",\"overview\":\"The interceptors make an early hour dash to catch a team of late night burglars and one of the suspects treats Liam to a full face of saliva. Jacko and Simon are in pursuit of a speeding driver who abandons the car and legs it.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-07-30\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Episode 13\",\"overview\":\"For the first time, pursuit is filmed from the suspect's perspective. Plus Liam and stiffer dog Louis help uncover thousands in cash and a £1/2 million of class A drugs. Finally, a 999 call causes firearms officers to rush to Guisborough at 11pm.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-10-29\",\"runtime\":45}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2008-05-09\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}